  (W, "The blockchain is the record in which Bitcoin's transactions are finally written down. The chapter calls it the distributed journal of all transactions and, in its opening overview, the consensus blockchain which is the authoritative journal of all transactions [AH]. The book's own chapter on the subject is more precise about the shape of the thing: the blockchain is the history of every confirmed transaction, and its data structure is an ordered, back-linked list of blocks of transactions, each block referring to the previous one [AH]. This third branch of the chapter is about how a transaction gets into that record and why, once it is there, it becomes progressively harder to remove."),
