  (W, "Mining is the process that turns a pool of unconfirmed transactions into the next block of the blockchain. The chapter introduces it in one sentence, saying that Alice's transaction does not become part of the blockchain until it is included in a block by a process called mining and that block has been validated by full nodes [AH]. This group gathers everything needed to read that sentence: who does the work, what they build, what makes the result valid, and what they are paid."),
