  (H, "The group is taken in the order in which a block is built. The miner is the specialized node that does the work. The candidate block is what it assembles from its memory pool. The proof of work is the search that makes the candidate valid, and its difficulty is adjusted so that the search takes about ten minutes across the whole network; the hash rate measures how fast that search is being run. The block and its header are the result, and the merkle tree is the device by which the small header commits to all the transactions. The consensus rules are what every node checks. The coinbase transaction and the block reward are how the miner is paid, and the mining pool is how a small miner gets paid regularly. The sudoku analogy closes the group as a teaching picture."),
