  (W, "A miner is a participant that builds candidate blocks and searches for the proof of work that would make one of them valid. The book's glossary defines a miner as a network node that finds valid proof of work for new blocks by repeated hashing [AH], and its mining chapter describes a concrete one: Jing, who earns bitcoin by running a mining rig, a specialized computer-hardware system designed to mine, connected to a server that runs a full node [AH]. A miner is therefore a full node with extra hardware and an extra job, not a different kind of participant."),
