  (E, "The chapter meets the block when the winning block containing Alice's transaction becomes part of the blockchain and counts as one confirmation of it, and it gives a link to the block so that a reader can look it up [AH]. The book's blockchain chapter lists the fields a stored block has: four bytes of block size, eighty bytes of header, a compact count of the transactions that follow, and then the transactions themselves [AH]."),
